.TH AD_L1L2 1 "2026-09-08" "ad 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ad_l1l2 \- find where ops start failing (L1/L2 bisect)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ad_l1l2
.I <oldfile>
.I <newfile>
.I <opsfile>
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ad_l1l2
applies the given op stream to the old file (using the C animator in
headless mode), then compares the resulting buffer against the new file
line-by-line. It reports:
.TP
.B L1
The last line where the buffer matches the new file (0 if line 1 already
differs). Everything up to L1 is confirmed correct.
.TP
.B L2
The first line where the buffer differs from the new file (0 if all lines
match). The bug starts at L2.
.TP
.B L_TOTAL
Total lines compared (max of buffer and new file).
.SH PURPOSE
This tool tests the **op stream** (produced by the diff engine + layer
chain), NOT the animator. The animator is the reference implementation
that applies ops. If the ops are correct, the animator produces correct
output. If the ops are wrong, L1/L2 pinpoints where.
.SH USAGE IN AD_SESSION
.B ad_session
runs L1/L2 automatically on session start and on ops.tsv save. The
result is shown in the status line:
.PP
.RS
L1/L2: ALL OK (123/123 lines match)
.br
L1/L2: OK 1-42, BAD at 43 (total 123)
.RE
.PP
Commands:
.TP
.B <leader>b
Re-run L1/L2 check manually.
.TP
.B <leader>f
Fold identical lines (folds lines 1..L1 in the result buffer).
.TP
.B <leader>t
Trim: create reduced files starting from L2 (prompts for prefix).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Check a single example:
.B ad_l1l2 old.py new.py ops.tsv
.TP
Check with a layer chain:
.B ad_postprocess --ad-layer=ad_layer_reorder < raw.tsv > post.tsv
.br
.B ad_l1l2 old.py new.py post.tsv
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ad (1),
.BR ad_session (1),
.BR ad_postprocess (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Written by the ad contributors.
